Rule 1 (reduction must be one of 'none', 'mean', or 'sum' to avoid invalid reduction values)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = "none" ∨ v_1 = "mean" ∨ v_1 = "sum"
>>
Rule 2 (delta must be strictly positive to avoid unsupported non-positive delta)
{v_2 : float} |= v_2 > 0
>>
Rule 3 (input and target must have identical, strictly positive shapes to avoid size-mismatch errors)
{v_3 : tensor, v_4 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_4) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_4, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (input and target must have the same floating-point dtype to avoid invalid casting to integer types)
{v_3 : tensor, v_4 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_3) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 8) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_4)
